   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "30-31 Petty Cury (Superdry), north side, faces SSE; x from the west end. 1920s-30s neo-Tudor ashlar range with three steep street gables (apexes rise above the eave; small slit lights in each gable not modelled). Upper storey: three recessed groups of stone-mullioned-and-transomed 3-light windows (lower lights tall, short transom lights above), one per gable. Ground: full-width dark-grey shopfront under a deep plain rendered fascia band with a projecting moulded ledge at ~4.4 m. Group positions estimated from oblique Geograph photos."
